<PARA INFOID = "T010251A083" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "8Dec2003"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Knock Sensor</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>A flat knock sensor has been adopted.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>Reliability is ensured by providing 1 sensors each on the left and right inside the V-bank.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4600017p" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "3.847in" />
</FIGURE>

<MECA ID = "T010251A083A301" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "12Dec2003"     MECATYPE = "ACTUATE" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Knock Sensor Operation</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>When the knock sensor receives vibration from the cylinder block, the movement of the weight lags due to inertia. As a result, pressure is applied to the piezoelectric ceramic provided between the cylinder block and the weight, generating voltage. The voltage is output almost constantly across all frequency bands, and the engine control computer detects the target frequency and determines that knocking is occurring.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4600029p" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "3.167in" />
</FIGURE>
</MECA>
</PARA>
</SECTION>